WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.580
- Over to our first
guest, she's had a storied

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.290
career with projects like
'Casino', 'Total Recall',

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.950
'Basic Instinct' and 'Ratchet' on Netflix.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.690
She just released a new memoir,

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.670
it's called 'The Beauty of Living Twice'.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.821
Lets say hello to Sharon Stone.

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:16.071
(applause)

00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:20.264
Hello, nice to meet you.

00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:24.460
- Oh my god, what a big
deal it is to meet you.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.493
- What? Are you serious?

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.000
- Yes it is a very big
deal for me to meet you.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.390
I just think you're amazing.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.470
- Oh, oh my god, I thought that was

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.850
going to go the opposite way.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.000
I am honored to have you on my show.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.833
How are you?

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:41.210
- You're so talented and

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.710
your music has had such
a powerful effect on

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.960
my life and I am such a huge fan.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.610
And you are so talented.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.923
- What is happening right now?

00:00:53.872 --> 00:00:56.715
I feel like I'm being pranked.

00:00:56.715 --> 00:01:00.360
I am so in awe of what you just said and

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.392
have no words. Which is
rare because I'm talkative.

00:01:03.392 --> 00:01:04.225
- Right.

00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:05.940
- Well, I have to mention this

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.510
because this just recently happened

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.900
so a well known singer recently posted

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.120
how inspired she is by you and I want

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.750
to bring this up because
I think its such a

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.810
beautiful thing when
you don't even realize

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.230
your impact, and you hear from someone,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.823
well maybe like what just
happened to me with you,

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.420
I had no idea that kind of impact.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.623
And Britney Spears wrote
something about you.

00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:29.143
Have you guys met before?

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:34.584
- Well Britney wrote to me
a very long and important

00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:38.510
poignant letter during a very
difficult time in her life

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.950
about the time when people
would recognize it for

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.626
whenever she shaved her
head wanting me to help her.

00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:48.435
I was in a very difficult time of my life.

00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:53.430
I couldn't help myself but
the truth of the matter is

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.060
we both needed help and she needed help

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.770
and I needed help and it's
the true fact of it is

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.830
it's very hard to be a
very successful woman

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.840
and not have everyone controlling you.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.197
Taking your finances and handling you.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:20.610
Women, and I'm sure all of
the young stars get handled.

00:02:21.499 --> 00:02:25.405
You get handled so much that,

00:02:25.405 --> 00:02:26.890
- There's a breaking point.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.440
- There is a huge breaking point

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.570
and there is a point where you get broken.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.403
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:32.888 --> 00:02:35.370
- And it's, the thing with Britney Spears

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.570
is so out of control and so awful

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.540
and you know I can say certainly it's been

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.760
very out of control and
awful more than once

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.813
in my life and I have certainly had it.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.950
It's very complicated to
take control of your life.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.570
It's very hard to get
control of your finances

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:01.210
and that's something that I'm
sure doesn't surprise you.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:05.030
- No, I literally - it's
such a cliched thing

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.280
because it does happen to everyone

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.924
that I've ever talked with.

00:03:08.924 --> 00:03:11.780
The funniest thing, if I ever write a book

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.635
which I probably never will.

00:03:12.635 --> 00:03:14.530
- You have to, because I
think it would be really good.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.233
- The only thing I will say is,

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.370
just being me was very difficult.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.010
People were, that is just being who I am.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.410
That's the most odd thing
I'll probably ever say

00:03:27.259 --> 00:03:28.510
but just having so many people tell you

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.910
who you should be and, "no, this sells"

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.517
and "you've got to do
this" "you can't say that"

00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:33.217
"Why did you talk about that?"

00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:35.440
"Well, they asked me, I don't know."

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.760
They try to put you in media training.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.920
I literally walked out of that thing.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.247
The guy looked at my manager and was like

00:03:40.247 --> 00:03:41.467
"Good luck."

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.630
Because I'm an open book and
I like being an open book

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:49.230
and I like being unfiltered
to a respectful point

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.580
obviously but it's just the craziest thing

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.850
for me and my experience was just being,

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.060
just being able to be me.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.240
And I feel like a lot
of people have their own

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.770
versions of that whenever
you're, you know,

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.030
in the public eye,
especially at a young age.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.447
But I agree, I think it needs to progress.

00:04:06.447 --> 00:04:07.298
(audience applauds)

00:04:07.298 --> 00:04:09.610
Her new book is called "The
Beauty of Living Twice"

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.160
so how did you come up with
the title for the book?

00:04:13.132 --> 00:04:16.790
Well, because when I had
the stroke and the nine day

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.620
blane bleed- brain bleed - blane bleed

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.976
(laughter)

00:04:21.976 --> 00:04:25.253
brain bleed, I did have that,

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.700
what they call the near death experience

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.873
which is actually like
you're dead and you're not.

00:04:31.873 --> 00:04:32.743
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.580
- Life is very different after that,

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.620
it's very very different.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.950
I've spent a lot of time with people

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.270
who had similar experiences
and I think we all

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:46.570
feel the same, that we're
still alive for a reason

00:04:47.802 --> 00:04:50.102
and that we have more
purpose driven lives now

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.430
and of course you're less fearful because

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.130
you've already died, so it's like,

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:56.963
what are you going to do?

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.130
Kill me again, I mean.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.140
I've been there and I
know what it looks like

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.440
and I'm not as afraid of
what you're going to do.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.726
You're going to threaten me,
you're going to do this to me,

00:05:07.726 --> 00:05:09.900
you're going to do that to me.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.203
Whatever, I'm already dead once.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.480
- I bet when that first happened though

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.740
were you terrified?

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.470
I've had friends, that
things have happened

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:20.480
that they were terrified
for the longest time

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.240
whether it's cancer,
whether it's an aneurism,

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:25.360
something happening to where
it's a near death experience.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.840
It's almost like, was
there a bit where you lived

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.420
in a little bit of fear because,
you know, you have family.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.283
- Oh, I couldn't have,
I could have done the

00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:37.490
triple cow sow and won
the gold medal in Olympics

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.510
of paranoia for probably a decade,

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.563
and still I can be triggered you know.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.790
- When you were recovering
from your aneurism

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.641
your son did something,
and I've had moments

00:05:51.641 --> 00:05:52.590
you know, moments in my life like that.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.160
A lot of people can relate to this.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.370
But what, what was the
moment that your son came in

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.880
and said something and
you were like, "whoa."

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.220
- It was the greatest thing
and he's still like this

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:06.060
going on 21, I was in bed,
I'd been in bed for months

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.120
and months and I was so
struggling, I was such a mess

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.960
and he came in, in his little onesie

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.910
and he's just standing
on the floor by my bed

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.540
and he looked at me and
he you know, waddled over

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.660
and pushed over the fireplace tools

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.920
and made this huge, just
like my head hurt so badly.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.117
And then he looks at me and he goes,

00:06:26.117 --> 00:06:29.753
"No more jammies, mommy. No more jammies"

00:06:31.025 --> 00:06:32.481
- I love that.

00:06:32.481 --> 00:06:34.290
- And I realized no matter how I felt,

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.570
he needed me to get my ass out of bed

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:41.040
and I was like, wow, okay.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.023
I have to be a mom no matter
what's happening to me.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.710
I don't think if he would have done that

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.360
I would have pushed
myself so hard to recover.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:55.360
You know, he's going to
be 21 and he is here, just

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:00.940
he is the most amazing
person and he is the most

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.640
full of self of discovery,
he's so evolved.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.607
He's such an evolved deep person.

00:07:07.607 --> 00:07:10.920
- That's a proud moment,
that's a proud moment

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:13.970
as a parent to have
parented a kid that ends up

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.410
like that.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.930
- [Sharon] I love my kids, it's
such an interesting journey.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.050
- There's nothing cooler.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:22.060
I mean I could win any
award or do whatever

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.990
there's nothing cooler than, first of all

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.640
my kid looking at me
and thinking I'm cool.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.877
That's the coolest thing, you're like,

00:07:27.877 --> 00:07:29.527
"okay I'm doing something right."

00:07:30.954 --> 00:07:32.990
So, what do you hope people
take away from this book?

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.670
Because it's a lot to write a book.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.550
I've had people ask me and
I'm like, "Oh God, I can't,

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.577
that's a lot of pressure."

00:07:38.577 --> 00:07:40.177
What do you hope they take away?

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:43.117
- Well I just hope that they understand

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.890
while it's not an easy
journey to come to terms

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:51.400
with yourself and you're
not going to come out of it

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.253
with the same people in your life.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.760
It's a valid and important
journey and it's a journey

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:02.640
that will leave you with your
feet firmly on the ground.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.760
You get to have yourself, you get yourself

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.170
at the end of a journey
of real self discovery

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:13.170
and real sincerity and you
will find as I've found,

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.140
you stop making up

00:08:16.881 --> 00:08:18.760
for your own,

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:22.060
the faults people say you have, you start,

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.192
you stop thinking I
have to fix everything,

00:08:25.192 --> 00:08:27.860
I have to fix everything for everybody,

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.040
I have to make everything okay

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.780
for everybody all the time.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:36.140
You end up thinking, if I'm okay,

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.940
if my feet are on the ground
then all the other adults

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.280
should be taking care of themselves too.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.530
- Yeah.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.560
- And when you finally
start giving back people

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:52.203
their own, you handle your own thing.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:58.070
You adult for yourself, people
will go berserk with that.

00:09:00.458 --> 00:09:01.390
Like, what do you mean you're not going

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.370
to be my

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.791
- [Kelly] Crutch.
- bum wiper?

00:09:04.791 --> 00:09:05.891
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- You know?

00:09:05.891 --> 00:09:07.290
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:10.730
- Then suddenly you're free to be present,

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.240
fully present in your own life,

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.877
then all those other great people

00:09:14.877 --> 00:09:18.060
who are present in their
own life are available

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:23.060
to hang out with you, so
you have a whole new life.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:25.710
- That's a hard thing
to do what you just said

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.630
is to break away from
those habits of trying

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:31.360
to help fix people or help them and then

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.193
you end up hurting them
because you become a crutch.

00:09:35.037 --> 00:09:38.449
And that's a hard thing
to do what you just said,

00:09:38.449 --> 00:09:39.981
- It is, especially when

00:09:39.981 --> 00:09:41.660
- So everybody should run to the bookstore

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:45.953
and purchase this book,
that's what I'm saying today.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.267
Well everybody, Sharon's book is called

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:51.260
"The Beauty of Living Twice"

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.353
You've got to check it out, it's out now.

